        <div class="text-xs text-slate-600 space-y-3 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          <p>
            PrivaSee evaluates mobile privacy through <strong class="text-slate-900">Contextual App Purpose Awareness</strong>, distinguishing between genuine operational requirements and suspicious surveillance:
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-[11px]">
            <div class="p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 text-blue-900">
              <strong class="text-blue-950 font-bold block mb-1">⭐ Core / Essential:</strong>
              Legitimate permissions required for core features (e.g. Camera in Instagram). Discounted risk penalty to avoid false alarms.
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 border border-slate-200 text-slate-800">
              <strong class="text-slate-900 font-bold block mb-1">🧩 Optional / Secondary:</strong>
              Adds convenience (e.g. friend syncing). Normal risk weight; safe to revoke without breaking the main app.
            </div>
            <div class="p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 border border-rose-200 text-rose-900">
              <strong class="text-rose-950 font-bold block mb-1">🚨 Suspicious / Spyware:</strong>
              Zero operational justification (e.g. Mic in Flashlight). Heavily penalized (1.6x threat multiplier).
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <i class="fa-solid fa-sliders text-emerald-600"></i>
              Modern Granular Mitigation Controls:
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-600">
              Rather than breaking apps with binary On/Off toggles, PrivaSee supports <strong class="text-slate-900">"While In Use Only"</strong> (foreground restriction) and <strong class="text-slate-900">"Approximate Location"</strong> (city-level masking) to drastically lower threat scores while preserving 100% app functionality.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-2 flex justify-end">
          <button id="btnDismissMethodologyModal" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white text-xs font-bold transition cursor-pointer">
